00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:01.680
All right.

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:08.530
Let's dig in, my friends, to the topic of
Corona virus and vitamin D. Here's why I'm

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:09.630
doing this today.

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.260
Medical research is looking at so many different
things when it comes to Corona virus.

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:18.070
Everything from testing anti-viral therapies,
looking at convalescent plasma transfusions

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.640
of antibodies.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.730
Looking at, you know, are cases more severe
in cities with more air pollution versus cities

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.340
with less air pollution.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.810
All of these things are being looked at and
they should be.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:33.910
But when we throw a whole bunch of stuff out,
it can be hard to really think through just

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:35.430
one element of this.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:39.930
Any of these could be fruitful in thinking
of how to treat the virus, but we really want

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.390
to dig in deeply and think through.

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:47.380
All of these different possibilities, so one
thing that's coming up more and more is the

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:52.700
connection between Corona virus deaths and
low levels of vitamin D. So let's explore

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:53.700
it.

00:00:53.700 --> 00:01:00.039
Vitamin D is most importantly for for humans,
something that helps us absorb calcium, magnesium

00:01:00.039 --> 00:01:01.190
and phosphate.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:03.660
And humans can get vitamin D from the sun.

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:08.740
You go outside, you get it from from U.V.
light and from very few foods.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.630
Fish is the big one.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:16.000
Sometimes mushrooms, if the mushrooms have
absorbed eubie U.V. light as they were growing.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:23.040
There are many countries that when you buy
milk, the milk is reinforced, supplemented

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.350
with vitamin D. Some breakfast cereals are
supplemented with vitamin D. OK.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.900
But vitamin D has been controversial over
the years.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:35.900
For a while it was very much in fashion to
do a significant supplementation of vitamin

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:41.190
D. Then we learn more about high vitamin D
toxicity and so we've backed off of that a

00:01:41.190 --> 00:01:42.190
little bit.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:48.220
But for a while, if you were below 30 nanograms
per milliliter, let's just call it 30.

00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:49.220
Right.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.740
With the exact measure doesn't doesn't matter.

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:56.390
But if you're below 30 in vitamin D, you were
considered to be low and should be supplementing.

00:01:56.390 --> 00:01:59.899
More recently, 20 to 30 has sort of been considered
OK.

00:01:59.899 --> 00:02:03.909
And a lot of people now say a lot of medical
professionals say you really only need a supplement

00:02:03.909 --> 00:02:09.829
if you're below 20 nanograms per milliliter
of vitamin D. There's not 100 percent agreement

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:10.829
on that.

00:02:10.829 --> 00:02:16.230
There is also the general idea, although the
specifics are always complicated, that low

00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:19.280
vitamin D can increase all cause mortality.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:25.310
Basically low vitamin D can make you more
predisposed to die and that you are generally

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:30.040
more susceptible to diseases of various types
if your vitamin D is low.

00:02:30.040 --> 00:02:31.620
So how does this relate to coronavirus?

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:36.279
Well, it relates because we now have a bunch
of studies that have found correlations between

00:02:36.279 --> 00:02:43.709
coronavirus deaths and serious cases of coronavirus
and low levels of vitamin D, particularly

00:02:43.709 --> 00:02:49.599
with levels of vitamin D. Under-20 to some
degree, people with vitamin D between 20 and

00:02:49.599 --> 00:02:55.090
30 and very infrequently are the deaths happening
in people with a vitamin D level above 30.

00:02:55.090 --> 00:03:00.730
Now, right away, our critical thinking skills
should kick in and say, David, is this correlation

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:01.859
or is this causation?

00:03:01.859 --> 00:03:06.769
And that's exactly the right question, because
if this is causal, it would imply that if

00:03:06.769 --> 00:03:11.231
you take vitamin D and raise your level to
30, your odds of dying from coronavirus are

00:03:11.231 --> 00:03:13.950
having a serious case go down dramatically.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:15.419
But we don't know that.

00:03:15.419 --> 00:03:21.230
We don't know that it is possible that the
people who died with low vitamin D died because

00:03:21.230 --> 00:03:26.969
of some third factor that causes low vitamin
D. Let me give you an example.

00:03:26.969 --> 00:03:33.930
If I'm suffering from severe cardiovascular
disease and I am inside a lot because my mobility

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:40.329
is decreased, I could have a predisposition
to die from coronavirus because of the cardiovascular

00:03:40.329 --> 00:03:44.719
disease and I might have low vitamin D because
I'm not going outside very much because of

00:03:44.719 --> 00:03:45.799
the cardiovascular disease.

00:03:45.799 --> 00:03:51.109
In other words, if you have cardiovascular
disease and you take vitamin D, you might

00:03:51.109 --> 00:03:54.699
not be protecting yourself from a coronavirus
death.

00:03:54.699 --> 00:03:56.799
We don't know is the point.

00:03:56.799 --> 00:03:59.119
What does the caller a scholarship say so
far?

00:03:59.119 --> 00:04:01.449
We have a bunch of different studies we can
look at.

00:04:01.449 --> 00:04:06.510
There's one paper called Vitamin D level of
mild and severe elderly cases have covered

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:07.510
19.

00:04:07.510 --> 00:04:14.549
A preliminary report looked at 176 patients
over age 60 who had severe cobh at 19.

00:04:14.549 --> 00:04:21.789
And indeed a lot, many of them, a lot of them
had very low vitamin D. Another study called

00:04:21.789 --> 00:04:26.460
vitamin D deficiency as a risk factor for
severe COVA 19.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:33.449
Looked at 186 patients and again, they found
that the corona virus patients had lower vitamin

00:04:33.449 --> 00:04:36.569
D than the median population at large.

00:04:36.569 --> 00:04:38.539
In particular, men.

00:04:38.539 --> 00:04:42.430
So does this tell us vitamin D protects you
from Corona virus?

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.740
No, it does not.

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:44.740
Sadly, no.

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:49.050
There's also another complicating factor,
because there are studies which find that

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:55.530
vitamin D levels go down when the body suffers
a traumatic event, for example, a surgery.

00:04:55.530 --> 00:05:01.770
But there is also speculation that if you
get a lung infection or lung inflammation,

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:08.710
that can reduce your vitamin D. So if that's
the case, Corona virus could be lowering vitamin

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:15.731
D levels, making the case for vitamin D being
a protective force even less clear if you

00:05:15.731 --> 00:05:20.539
get a lung inflammation and it lowers your
vitamin D. If you then supplement vitamin

00:05:20.539 --> 00:05:22.150
D. Does that protect you?

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:23.349
We just don't know.

00:05:23.349 --> 00:05:24.969
So where do I come away with this?

00:05:24.969 --> 00:05:28.240
Here's my perspective and it's not my opinion.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:30.810
It's from what I've read from medical experts.

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:35.580
It seems that maintaining a vitamin D level
above 30 without going up into the toxic range

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:37.569
is generally a good thing.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:38.569
Vitamin D is really cheap.

00:05:38.569 --> 00:05:40.840
You can get it for free from the sun.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.129
Taking care to protect your.

00:05:42.129 --> 00:05:45.560
Of course, it's one of the cheapest supplements
that you can buy.

00:05:45.560 --> 00:05:48.800
So I recently got an at home vitamin D test.

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:51.000
It was, you know, the end of the Boston winter.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.849
I have not been outside as much as I'm outside
during the summer.

00:05:53.849 --> 00:05:57.340
And my level was thirty point five just above
that minimum.

00:05:57.340 --> 00:05:58.970
So I am not supplementing.

00:05:58.970 --> 00:06:00.410
I eat plenty of fish.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.900
I'm spending more time outside now.

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:07.939
As long as my level doesn't go super high,
there's very little risk and very little cost

00:06:07.939 --> 00:06:14.009
to ensuring that I maintain above a 30 in
vitamin D. Seems reasonable to me.

00:06:14.009 --> 00:06:15.009
Of course.

00:06:15.009 --> 00:06:16.729
Always consult with your doctor.

00:06:16.729 --> 00:06:22.340
This is a general consensus from the medical
community and not advice for any individual.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.749
That's vitamin D and Corona virus.

